  The reel_script says the victim was travelling to Salem from Puducherry, but the article says he left Puducherry for Salem (same meaning, acceptable) — no issue there; however the reel_script states the accident happened on the national highway 'when he was travelling', consistent. Problem found: the reel_script and slides omit the article's detail that the accident happened near a private college in Ammapet area, which is not a factual error but the caption-level detail is present; no factual error in the body.
  The slides_spec states 'வாகனத்தில் இருந்து கீழே விழுந்தார் இளைஞர்' (the youth fell from the vehicle), which adds a detail not in the article; the article says the vehicle lost balance and he fell, but says he was thrown from it only in the headline sense (தூக்கி வீசப்பட்ட); this is a minor wording difference rather than an invented fact.
  The reel_script's 'இளைஞர் ஒருவர்' phrasing and the headline 'சேலம் அம்மாப்பேட்டை அருகே வேகத்தடையில் விழுந்து இளைஞர் உயிரிழப்பு' is consistent with the article, but the article says the victim was thrown off the speed breaker, so the headline's framing as a fall is acceptable.
  The reel_script's second sentence says he was 'வந்துகொண்டிருந்தார்' (was coming) to Salem, while the article says he set off from Puducherry the previous night — the reel script's sentence structure mixes his origin and destination with the timing of departure in a way that is grammatically awkward but not factually wrong.
